# Cloudflare R2 credentials for the auction-analysis image store.
#
#   cp .env.r2.example .env.r2   &&   edit .env.r2
#
# .env.r2 is gitignored. Do not commit it, and do not paste these values
# into a chat window or an issue.
#
# Where each value comes from:
#
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID  Cloudflare dashboard -> R2 -> the 32-hex-character string
#                  in your S3 API endpoint, or in the browser URL after
#                  /accounts/. NOT the bucket name.
#
#   R2_BUCKET      The bucket you created.
#
#   R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
#                  R2 -> API -> Manage API tokens -> Create API token.
#                  Permission: "Object Read & Write". Scope it to this one
#                  bucket. The secret is shown exactly once — copy it then.
#
#                  An R2 *API token* (the long single string) is not the same
#                  thing as the Access Key ID / Secret pair. The S3 endpoint
#                  needs the key pair; take those from the same screen.

R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_BUCKET=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
